  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 843 PM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nThrough the long term forecast, mid level ridging to our southwest\nwill dampen, keeping troughing to our east as the primary influence\nfor local weather. The dampening ridge paired with persistent\ntroughing along the east coast will maintain northwest flow aloft\nthrough the period. This will maintain our cooler and drier airmass\nwith temperatures remaining in the mid to high 80s each day. The next\nfeature of interest looks to arrive at the end of the long term in\nthe form of a passing mid level trough and associated surface cold\nfront. Along and ahead of this front, light southerly surface flow\nlooks to induce some weak return flow which may allow us to briefly\nbreak back into the 90s on Tuesday, this however is contingent on the\nactual timing of the front. If the front speeds up, associated cloud\ncover and slight increases in rain chances may keep highs on Tuesday\nbelow 90. Currently kept blended guidance for rain chances, which\nsupport the front passing through on Wednesday with highest rain\nchances Wednesday afternoon. With this being about a week out, timing\nand impacts from the front are likely to change, please check back\nfor updates.",
